  "scope": "Stage4J4: D3D9 VB stream and IB binding holds separate from public resource refs, public0->1/1->0 transitions pin/release one device ref, and physical storage survives while any private slot remains. Shared VB/IB storage destructors unlink, clear private data, free clip records and shadows before releasing the public device pin last. Live replacement publishes new slots/properties before old storage release. Device cleanup, primitive-UP stream0 clearing and indexed-UP stream0/indices clearing all drop private holds. DEFAULT Reset blockers read public refs/locks without private stream/index discounts; recording/stateblock retains existing public hold semantics. Native actual methods with constructors/emitters:91904 new checks,1024 pool/order profiles,16384 public-zero revivals,three VB streams/oneIB slot,isolated VB/IB public Reset blockers,UP helpers and shadow/clip teardown;27 strictly compiled runtime-assertion mutants,old actual methods plus new helper runtime negative control and ASAN/UBSAN. Retains2D/cube/volume/standalone actual lifetime suites. Real XP creates3VB/2IB,256 buffer revivals and256 private-data queries with exact device pins; public-zero indexed draws use stream offset16 then partial vertex update; primitiveUP retires only bound VB and retains IB, indexedUP retires both bound buffers, referenced VB/IB separately block Reset, binding-only buffers allow Reset and post-Reset readback. Six exact buffer uploads,two bound indexed draws,one primitiveUP,one indexedUP,one clear and five real readbacks have simulated transport pixels; independent GPU replay validates320 pixels and all five explicit buffer destructions acrossUP/Reset,with empty guest maps before genuine owner release. Clip allocation/release surrounding native methods is a constructor callback stub; actual software clipping algorithms retain their independent regressions. NULL-stream offset/stride retail quirks,D3D8/declaration/shader/stateblock binding refs,general external-child root-state retention,arbitrary callbacks/thread/loss/full Reset/format/MSAA/fullscreen/multi-buffer/wrapper conversion,native HAL,games/FPS and overall stages4/5/6 remain open. Host/protocol/shader/bundle and D3D8/DDraw unchanged.",
